        "original_id": "0c8b73ab-357c-588a-92ce-3dc4a751c2a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Grand Hyatt New York, Grand Central Terminal, Midtown Manhattan, New York City\n- Buildings: Commodore Hotel\n- People: Donald Trump\n- Roles: President of the United States\n- Events: 1945 NFL Draft\n\nFacts:\n- The Commodore Hotel in New York City was originally built and opened on January 28, 1919.\n- The 1945 NFL Draft was held on April 8, 1945, at the Commodore Hotel in New York City, New York.\n- Donald Trump was born on June 14, 1946.\n- In 1980, Donald Trump modernized the outside of the Commodore Hotel building and renovated its inside as part of his first construction project in Manhattan.\n- Donald Trump became the 45th President of the United States on January 20, 2017.\n- The Grand Hyatt New York is a hotel located directly east of Grand Central Terminal in Midtown Manhattan, New York City.\n- The Grand Hyatt New York was originally built as the Commodore Hotel.",
